   (IC3E), Shanghai, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAR 14-16, 2019},
Organization = {Int Soc Environm Informat Sci; Asia Pacific Inst Sci \& Engn; Xiamen
   Univ Technol; Fujian Smart City Assoc},
Abstract = {Indoor air pollution has been a severe problem in China since the 1970s.
   Currently, the primary indoor air pollutants are PM2.5 and PM10 in
   China. This study has investigated the PM performance inside a case
   study apartment, and the correlations between the indoor PM
   concentrations and the ambient PM concentrations have been identified
   and analysed. The results indicated that the indoor PM concentrations
   could not meet the requirements of the China Indoor Air Quality Standard
   (GBT18883-2012). The inside particulate matters were mainly originating
   from the ambient environment. Moreover, plants could reduce the indoor
   PM concentrations in a stable indoor environment during the unoccupied
   period, and the cleaning efficiency can be increased by install as many
   plants as possible into the space.},
