   (ICEEP 2013), Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, APR 19-21, 2013},
Organization = {Inner Mongolia Univ; Chinese Acad Sci, Res Ctr Eco Environm Sci, Key Lab
   Environm Biotechnol},
Abstract = {During the process of urbanization, impermeable surface areas enlarge
   and rain runoff and peak discharges grow, rainstorm become more
   frequent. As more rain water and pollutants mixed with each other, more
   areas of urban runoff are polluted, causing significant change to
   aquatic organisms, especially fish, their population and structure. In
   order to balance the relations between urban development and river
   eco-environmental protection, avoid reappearance of mega rainstorm
   disaster like the one on July 21st in Beijing, we suggest protecting and
   safeguarding the structure and function of urban river ecological system
   from perspectives of urban planning, eco-environment improvement and
   integrated management over urban river system.},
