   HSE},
Abstract = {Water pollution is one of the biggest environmental problems in India.
   Industrialization and urbanization had increased contamination in the
   water bodies. Over past few decades, the improper disposal of hazardous
   waste and electronic waste and toxic effluent had increased heavy metal
   contamination and physicochemical parameter in surface and groundwater
   bodies. The objectives of this research paper are to assess the heavy
   metals and physicochemical parameter in surface and groundwater in
   different land use pattern, i.e. industrial area, agricultural area and
   urban area. The surface water samples were collected from different
   streams and rivers and groundwater samples were collected from tubewell,
   well and borewells during summer season, pre-monsoon season and
   post-monsoon season. The parameters like pH, DO, temperature,
   conductivity, bicarbonate, fluoride and heavy metals Fe, Pb, Cu, Zn, Cd,
   Cr, As, Sr and B were analyzed in the laboratory.},
