   International-Association-for-Engineering-Geology-and-the-Environment,
   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {Regional news testify how the Palermo Plain has been subjected to
   disastrous floods since ancient times. The principal causes of flooding
   lie in the inadequate scale of hydraulic works, and in the influence of
   ancient river-beds, minor water courses and natural ditches. To these
   factors, we must also add the physical characteristics of the territory,
   climatic conditions, unplanned urban expansion. To safeguard the urban
   environment the principal actions to be realised are: the construction
   of the new storm drain already designed for the: protection of the newly
   urbanised areas and intervention on the Oreto river that covers
   construction of a dyke which allows slow dispersion of the flood and of
   a tunnel to carry overflow directly to the sea and widening the river
   bed cross-section.},
