   (GBSC), Bologna, ITALY, SEP 15-16, 2011},
Abstract = {The roads often cross territories dividing them according to logical
   entirely extraneous to their nature, because belonging to other places
   to be connected, but they can become also new axes of attraction on the
   trace of which the environment is modified, other layouts are directed,
   the constructions are prepared, suburbs and cities are born. One think
   about the road especially for what it conducts to see, often forgetting
   us that itself is something to see, it is a constitutive element of the
   prominent characters of a certain place. It is necessary therefore to
   review the forms and the ways of the road-layouts arranged to the
   lightening of the urban traffic and to the installation of new
   districts, doing so that their sustainability is environmental above all
   and it can contribute to the construction of a new landscape. An
   exemplification of such attitude can be seen in the proposal of
   fast-flowing road layout arranged to a substantial urbanization in the
   delicate scenery of the Venetian lagoon. (C) 2011 Published by Elsevier
