Abstract = {Evidence-based medicine implies that randomised controlled trials,
   meta-analyses and systematic reviews will be used by clinicians to
   determine the most appropriate therapy for patients. Cochrane reviews
   are the prototype of systematic reviews, but they are not optimally
   utilised by physicians in the United States. This may be related to lack
   of access, unfamiliarity with the format, and the perception that they
   are impractical for actual patient care. An opportunity exists to
   criticise and improve systematic reviews, and changes are suggested to
   make them more user-friendly.},
