   Semarang, INDONESIA, AUG 03-04, 2016},
Abstract = {The awareness to do firm social function is generally stated and
   represented in the form of expenditure ( cost) of corporate social
   responsibility (CSR). The objective of this research was to test the
   effect of corporate governance effectiveness on CSR disclosure and to
   test the effect of CSR disclosure on capital constraint, value
   relevance, and investor's perception on firm. This research uses
   regression analysis. Data obtained was from Indonesian Stock Exchange
   (IDX) listed banking firms for the year 2008-2012. Total sample of this
   research was 68 firms. The result showed that corporate governance
   effectiveness significantly having positive relation on CSR disclosure
   and investor's perception but has negative relation with capital
   constraint. In addition, the research shows no significant result
   indicating CSR disclosure is value relevance.},
