Note = {4th Euro-Mediterranean Conference for Environmental Integration-EMCEI,
   Sousse, TUNISIA, NOV 01-04, 2022},
Abstract = {Being part of the urban green infrastructure of cities, historic gardens
   and cultural landscapes hold major positive impacts on urban landscapes'
   sustainability and biodiversity; however, the efficiency of the
   traditional heritage conservation solutions seems degrading due to the
   climate change impacts and the contemporary challenges including massive
   tourism, maintenance issues, and social challenges. Therefore, new
   durable, sustainable and ecosystem friendly solutions should be
   implemented. This paper discusses the possibilities of improving the
   quality of historic gardens' ecosystem and its impacts on the
   biodiversity and enhancement of the urban environment. The study method
   consists of discussing the theoretical background of renewal strategies;
   the evaluation of practical examples of several newly adapted
   sustainable solutions and their integration in their immediate
   environment; lastly, presenting the applied sustainable solutions for
   the maintenance of the green elements of Al-Hambra gardens in Spain and
   enhancing the impacts of climate change in the Mediterranean and
   semi-arid region. Based on the studied examples and the literature
   background, this research sorts out the most efficient and applicable
   solutions for adaptation in similar contexts of historic gardens.},
