   Silesian Region},
Booktitle = {PROCEEDINGS OF THE 12TH EUROPEAN CONFERENCE ON MANAGEMENT, LEADERSHIP
   AND GOVERNANCE (ECMLG 2016)},
Series = {Proceedings of the Conference on European Management Leadership and
   Governance},
Year = {2016},
Pages = {116-124},
Note = {12th European Conference on Management, Leadership and Governance
   (ECMLG), Natl Univ Polit Studies \& Publ Adm, Coll Management,
   Bucharest, ROMANIA, NOV 10-11, 2016},
Abstract = {Risk management in post transition economies still requires improvement
   in the area of techniques and methods. Therefore, the main aim of this
   article is to present the results of surveys completed by Polish
   managers from the Silesian region identifying the risk perception and
   risk management methods in Polish enterprises. The results allow for the
   formulation of recommendations concerning the development of Enterprise
   Risk Management systems in the conditions of Polish economy. The article
   is divided into three parts. The first part includes the literature
   studies on risk perception and ERM systems. The second part presents the
   research methodology. The third part consists of research results and
   findings on Polish managers. The main conclusion is that Polish managers
   are afraid of risk and its consequences but they do not know the methods
   of risk management and they rarely use ERM systems. Apart from risk
   financing and transferring it, they do not widely recognize other
   methods of risk management. Their risk attitude is rather passive; thus,
   they need to be educated about risk management techniques.},
