   the Case of the Biella Province in Italy},
Booktitle = {III INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON LANDSCAPE AND URBAN HORTICULTURE},
Series = {Acta Horticulturae},
Year = {2013},
Volume = {999},
Pages = {153-157},
Note = {3rd International Conference on Landscape and Urban Horticulture,
   Nanjing, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 29-JUL 03, 2011},
Organization = {Int Soc Hort Sci},
Abstract = {The valorisation and the conservation of the historic gardens and parks
   is a strong issue in Europe, as the need to keep such a heritage alive
   is very up to date. This paper presents a project that is indeed about
   the proposal of a new way of facing the problem and it is referred to
   the case study of the Biella province, in Piedmont in the north-west of
   Italy. A thorough survey of the gardens and the nurseries was carried
   out to assess a precise state of the art of the green heritage of the
   Biella province and on the base of the gathered information a series of
   criteria were set out for the itineraries. Seven itineraries were set,
   of two types: theme itineraries (corresponding to one criterion) and
   transversal itineraries (grouping more criteria). Each itinerary was
   also associated with one or more nurseries presenting characteristics
   that were inherent with the route theme or were historically linked to
   the gardens. This work can be considered as a starting point for making
   owners, nurserymen and tourists aware of the historical parks
   conservation issue.},
