   Management},
Abstract = {With the opportunity to be set as the comprehensive trial place of
   resource-saving and environment-friendly society, leisure agriculture in
   Changsha City is very likely to become a new point of regional economic
   growth. However, despite of resident's strong desire for leisure
   products, the actual consumption on leisure agriculture was less than
   10\% of the total spending on agriculture products. Hence, how to
   promote the latent demand to effective one is the key for the healthy
   development of leisure agriculture. To explore demand constraints in it,
   this study took Changsha City as an example, and conducted a survey on
   customer behaviors and satisfaction toward leisure agriculture products.
   Liken Scale was used to measure customer satisfaction in term of five
   dimensions of tourism service quality. Also some managerial implications
   to firms were discussed based on the detailed analysis of the survey
   results.},
