Abstract = {The urban heat island phenomenon is one of the important problems faced
   by the metropolitan environment in hot-summer and cold-winter areas. In
   order to conduct truthful and in-depth analysis on this phenomenon, this
   study covers temperature data acquisition and a series of data collation
   and analysis conducted with the mobile testing method, more actually
   reflects theheat islandspatial-temporal changes from the central area of
   Wuhan in Winter to the urban fringe, analyzes the urban morphology,
   urban underlying surfacecharacteristics, and impacts of human factors
   and microclimate, and explores the feasible quantification basis for
   urban design and planning.},
