   Dev Holdings Ltd; K C Wong Educ Fdn; Environm \& Conservat Fund; Gammon;
   Paul Y; Architecture Design \& Res Grp Ltd (AD+RG); China State
   Construct (CSCEC); Sino Grp; Vantage Int (Holdings) Ltd; ASCE Hong Kong
   Sect; ASHRAE Hong Kong Chapter; CIBSE; Construct Ind Council (CIC);
   Chartered Inst Bldg (CIOB); Council Sustainable Dev; Emerald; Hong Kong
   Inst Architects; Hong Kong Institut Engineers; Hong Kong Inst Surveyors;
   HKSTS; IUE; JSCE; RICS; Urban Planning Soc China; China Civil Engn Soc;
   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {Recently, the effective uses of various industrial by-products and
   wastes are requested in Japan. In this study, authors paid attention to
   sewage sludge incinerated ash which was emitted from sewage-works, the
   strength, carbonation and leaching in concrete using the ash were
   considered to clarify the effectiveness as a part of fine aggregate for
   concrete. In this study the strength test, accelerated carbonation test
   and leaching test were carried out with concrete specimen using the ash.
   The replacement ratios of the ash were 0, 5 and 10\% for volume of fine
   aggregate. The method of leaching test was prescribed in JSCE Standard
   JSCE-G 575-2005. Test was carried out with using cylindrical specimen,
   which had no crack. The following conclusions were obtained from the
   experimental results. 1) The compressive strength and carbonation in
   concrete with sewage sludge incinerated ash did not have bad effects at
   the range of replacement ratio from 5\% to 10\%. 2) Fluorine was
   released a little on leaching test, but other elements such as boron,
   hexavalent chromium, arsenic, seleniummercury, cadmium, mercury and
   lead, were not released more than the minimum value that was able to be
   measured. The results were satisfied with the environmental quality
   standards of the reclamation, the water quality and the drainage in all
   elements. The development of the usage in the future could be expected
   from these results.},
